  "tagline": "Managed, distributed SQLite with pub/sub, edge functions and CRDT sync to on-device databases.",
  "description": "SQLite Cloud is a managed service that runs SQLite databases on a Raft-replicated cluster and exposes them over its own protocol, HTTP and WebSockets, with users and roles, built-in pub/sub, edge functions and backups. The company, now branded SQLite AI, also publishes SQLite extensions: SQLite-Sync for CRDT-based offline sync between local SQLite and the cloud (or Postgres and Supabase), SQLite-Vector for vector search and SQLite-AI for on-device inference. It suits teams who want SQLite semantics end to end, from device to server, without operating replication themselves.",
